{"kind":"ignore","path":"configs/site-held-addresses.jsonl","reason":"This list: it holds every address by definition and is read by the check as the list, not scanned as a holder."}
{"kind":"ignore","path":"*.html","reason":"Site pages the host serves from the repository root; their own links are resolved by tests/site_links_test.go and the page set by scripts/doc-registry.ps1, so they are the site, not an outside surface."}
{"kind":"ignore","path":"[a-z][a-z]/index.html","reason":"The ten per-language landings the host serves; the same gates as the root pages hold them, so they are the site, not an outside surface."}
{"kind":"ignore","path":"sitemap.xml","reason":"Generated from docs/DOCUMENT_REGISTRY.jsonl by scripts/doc-registry.ps1 -Generate and compared with it on every run; a render target, never hand-edited."}
{"kind":"ignore","path":"robots.txt","reason":"A file the host serves that names the sitemap by its absolute address; scripts/doc-registry.ps1 reads that address as the site base, so it is the source of the base rather than a holder."}
{"kind":"ignore","path":"DEV/**","reason":"Engineering ledgers, commit log, dated research and archived notes: records of what was true when written, read by no user and no program. DEV/RELEASE.md mentions the sitemap address as a release step that scripts/release.ps1, which is listed, performs."}
